      "review_notes": "The previously reviewed independent tree law is identified with Mathlib Poisson(1). A single rank-kernel expectation combines absorption and the auxiliary size-minus-boundary termination potential; expected auxiliary credit contracts at size>=2. CTE uses one uniform rank followed by obvious stop/up/down cases, fixed-credit amplification, and an initial literal step. Infinite continuation values never enter real arithmetic. Independent clients check framing, infinite expectation, and the canonical zero atom exp(-1)."
    }
